@startuml
title Save/Load Job Applications Persistently in the Database

autonumber

actor Student
participant "Frontend UI\n(React / JobTracker)" as UI
participant "REST API\n(Express server/app.ts)" as API
participant "Data Access Layer\n(applicationRepository / Prisma)" as DAL
database "SQLite Database" as DB

note over UI,DB
The API-backed sequence below reflects the endpoints and repository calls
implemented in server/app.ts and server/applicationRepository.ts.
The current JobTracker implementation still uses src/lib/storage.ts
(localStorage) and must call these endpoints to use SQLite persistence.
end note

== Create and save an application ==

Student -> UI: Enter application details\nand select "Save application"
UI -> UI: Validate form fields\n(validateApplication)

alt Client-side validation fails
  UI --> Student: Display field errors\n(no request sent)
else Input is valid
  UI -> API: POST /api/applications\nJSON ApplicationInput
  activate API
  API -> DAL: toApplicationInput(req.body)
  DAL --> API: Normalized ApplicationInput
  API -> DAL: createApplication(input)
  activate DAL
  DAL -> DAL: Validate status and jobType\nand validateApplication(input)

  alt Repository validation fails
    DAL --> API: throw ValidationError
    deactivate DAL
    API --> UI: 400 { errors }
    deactivate API
    UI --> Student: Display validation errors
  else Input is valid
    DAL -> DB: INSERT JobApplication\nand related StatusChange
    activate DB

    alt Database write fails
      DB --> DAL: Database error
      deactivate DB
      DAL --> API: Propagate error
      deactivate DAL
      API -> API: Log error
      API --> UI: 500 { error }
      deactivate API
      UI --> Student: Display save failure
    else Write succeeds
      DB --> DAL: Created row with timeline\n(include ordered by id)
      deactivate DB
      DAL -> DAL: Map row to Application
      DAL --> API: Application
      deactivate DAL
      API --> UI: 201 Created\nApplication JSON
      deactivate API
      UI --> Student: Show saved application\nand success message
    end
  end
end

== Load applications ==

Student -> UI: Open or refresh Job Tracker
UI -> API: GET /api/applications
activate API
API -> DAL: listApplications()
activate DAL
DAL -> DB: SELECT JobApplication rows\ninclude StatusChange timeline\norder by createdAt DESC
activate DB

alt Database read fails
  DB --> DAL: Database error
  deactivate DB
  DAL --> API: Propagate error
  deactivate DAL
  API -> API: Log error
  API --> UI: 500 { error }
  deactivate API
  UI --> Student: Display load failure
else Read succeeds
  DB --> DAL: Rows with timelines
  deactivate DB
  DAL -> DAL: Map each row to Application
  DAL --> API: Application[]
  deactivate DAL
  API --> UI: 200 OK\nApplication[] JSON
  deactivate API
  UI --> Student: Render application list
end

== API error handling ==

note over API
Express error middleware maps:
- ValidationError -> 400 { errors }
- NotFoundError -> 404 { error }
- Invalid JSON SyntaxError -> 400
- Other errors -> 500 { error } and console.error
end note

@enduml